cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: morphline
abstract: >-
  A BIDS-aware longitudinal neuroimaging derivatives pipeline. morphline ingests
  FreeSurfer .stats output, accounts for every observation it gains and loses
  against an attributable-loss funnel, applies three-level quality control,
  harmonizes across scanners with an in-repo ComBat implementation, fits
  longitudinal linear mixed-effects models over a declared 28-test region set
  with separately corrected FDR families, and emits a self-contained HTML report
  carrying the provenance needed to reconstruct the run. The longitudinal path
  is validated against synthetic ground truth with injected effects; real-data
  integration (ABIDE PCP) is cross-sectional and validates ingestion, QC, and
  harmonization only.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Matt
    family-names: Glittenberg
repository-code: "https://github.com/mattglittenberg/morphline"
url: "https://mattglittenberg.github.io/morphline/"
license: MIT
